NCT06966830.elig:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. Age 4-60 years old, gender is not limited;
2. Status epilepticus meets the 2015 diagnostic criteria of the International League Against Epilepsy, i.e., a state of persistent seizures that may cause long-term impairment and manifests itself as:

(1) Tonic-clonic seizures or convulsive seizures, lasting \> 5min; (2) Between 2 or more seizures, consciousness is not restored; (3) Focal seizures with impaired consciousness, lasting \>10min; (4) absence seizures, lasting \>15min; 3. Informed consent of the patient and signed a written consent form.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Unstable vital signs;
2. Electrocardiogram showing atrial flutter, atrial fibrillation, second-degree, third-degree atrioventricular block;
3. History of allergy to the drugs used this time;
4. Participants have a known history of past or present illness of non-epileptic seizures, and current seizures cannot be judged as status epilepticus based on symptomatology and/or electroencephalogram;
5. Other patients who are considered by the investigator to be unsuitable to participate in the study;
6. Incomplete clinical data or follow-up information

